        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Manage Claw cron jobs through the gateway",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- install grouped Claw cron declarations through the gateway-owned cron.add API\n- persist pending, complete, or failed ownership references keyed by the final agent id and declaration id\n- expose cron ownership in status, round-trip complete declarations through export, and remove scheduler jobs before agent config\n- keep ambiguous pending or failed ownership visible and block destructive cleanup until it is reconciled\n\n## Contract\n\n- scheduler mutation stays in the gateway; Claws never write the cron store directly\n- declaration keys are scoped as claw:<agent-id>:<manifest-job-id>, so package-local ids do not collide globally\n- cron.add results may be direct jobs or declaration-convergence results\n- main declarations map to the final agent named main session, while isolated/current remain explicit\n\n## Verification\n\n- pnpm tsgo:core\n- 27 focused cron, lifecycle, export, and CLI tests\n- 9 provenance/add tests\n- emitted cron.add payload validated by the gateway protocol validator\n\nStacked on #102306. Experimental CLI remains gated by OPENCLAW_EXPERIMENTAL_CLAWS=1.",
